firebase-debug.log
*.log
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
# Plan Review Gate artifacts — per-session Combined-verdict handoff state, never committed
.verdicts/
**/.DS_Store

# Claude Code local settings — machine-specific, may hold tokens/paths. Never commit
# (COREDEV-2486, audit critic.1: same accidental-commit class as the firebase-debug.log incident).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Transient reviewer artifacts (per-invocation, not source of truth).
# GLOBS, not exact names: a multi-round gate writes `.agy-prompt-<ticket>r<n>.md`, and the
# exact-name entries here once matched none of those — so `git add -A` committed 16 of them into a
# release commit (COREDEV-2597).
#
# Then it happened AGAIN (COREDEV-2642): `.agy-prompt*`/`.codex-prompt*` match neither
# `.codex-impl-*.md` nor `.kimi-prompt-pr63.md`, and `git add -A` committed 17 more. Narrowing by
# the second word is what failed twice — these are named after the TOOL, and each tool grows new
# suffixes (`-prompt`, `-impl`, whatever a future round needs). Ignore by tool prefix instead, so a
# new suffix is covered on the day it is invented rather than after it lands in a commit.
.agy-*.md
.codex-*.md
.kimi-*.md
.gate-*-prompt.md

# Python bytecode (MCP review-synthesizer is stdlib Python)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Hook state/logs (COREDEV-2324/2325). Markers, diagnostic logs, compaction snapshots,
# and reviewer captures live under the plugin data dir (~/.claude/unleashed-mail),
# outside the repo — these entries are defensive, in case state ever lands in-tree.
.state/
logs/
*.jsonl
reviews/

# Test fixture trees, created in the REPO ROOT by tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=REPO)
# (COREDEV-2642, PR #63 review gap 23). These hold DELIBERATELY WEAKENED COPIES of the gate
# scripts — mutation proofs need the mutant to sit where the real one does. A killed run leaves
# them behind, and a later `git add -A` then commits a weakened gate: exactly the COREDEV-2597
# incident. Cleanup is `addCleanup`-based and so does not survive SIGKILL, which is why these
# are ignored rather than merely tidied up.
#
# All SEVEN prefixes are listed, not just the five the review cited — the same hazard applies to
# every fixture rooted in the repo, and a partial list is how the next one gets missed.
.callers-default-mutant-*/
.callers-selection-mutant-*/
.callers-shallow-*/
.m4-freshness-proof-*/
.m5-wrapper-proof-*/
.thread-proof-*/
.wrapper-proof-*/
